  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Marine turtle monitoring in Conkouati-Douli National Park (CDNP), Republic of Congo: 2014-2015 Season</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will conduct training for community members that will support a leatherback conservation program along 57 km of leatherback nesting beach within Conkouati-Douli National Park, which is contiguous with the major leatherback nesting population in Mayumba National Park, Gabon. This grant will also support marine enforcement patrols by the Park in the waters extending 3 miles from the Parks shoreline to deter illegal foreign industrial fishing vessels, which are the cause of much of the sea turtle bycatch mortality within the Park.nsure the implementation of daily nest surveys and protection activities within the Park, work with local communities and fisherman to minimize sea turtle bycatch from coastal gill net fisheries, and conduct marine patrols with Park vessel to deter illegal industrial fishing within Park waters.</narrative>
  </description>
